# Three changes to cowrie_plugin.py:
#
#   CHANGE 1 — top-level import (after existing cowrie.telnet.factory import)
#     import cowrie.http.factory
#
#   CHANGE 2 — __init__() reads enableHTTP from config
#     Matches the pattern for self.enableSSH and self.enableTelnet.
#     Add after the self.enableTelnet block:
#       self.enableHTTP: bool = CowrieConfig.getboolean(
#           "http", "enabled", fallback=False
#       )
#
#   CHANGE 3 — pool_ready() wires HTTP factory at end of method
#     Add after the closing lines of the Telnet block.
#     See pool_ready_addition.py for the exact indented block.
#
# Note on the startup validation in makeService():
#   if not self.enableTelnet and not self.enableSSH and not self.pool_only:
#       print("ERROR: You must at least enable SSH or Telnet...")
#       sys.exit(1)
#   HTTP is not included in this check — intentional. HTTP is always
#   deployed alongside SSH in THIR's configuration, so this check is
#   never a problem. If HTTP-only deployment is ever needed, this check
#   would need a third condition: and not self.enableHTTP.
#   Not required for current THIR deployment.
